quote", "source": {"url": "https://www.statssa.gov.za/publications/P0211/P02112ndQuarter2025.pdf", "title": "Quarterly Labour Force Survey, Quarter 2: 2025 (P0211)", "publisher": "Statistics South Africa", "pageNumber": null, "publishedOn": "2025-08-12", "sectionLabel": "Key findings", "versionLabel": "P0211 · Q2 2025", "referencePeriod": "Q2 2025 (April–June 2025)", "sourceVersionId": "7f6529fe-625a-4ada-808e-78d62ccf97a1"}}, {"text": "The number of unemployed persons rose to 8.4 million in Q2 2025, from 8.2 million in Q1 2025.", "type": "official_quote", "source": {"url": "https://www.statssa.gov.za/publications/P0211/P02112ndQuarter2025.pdf", "title": "Quarterly Labour Force Survey, Quarter 2: 2025 (P0211)", "publisher": "Statistics South Africa", "pageNumber": null, "publishedOn": "2025-08-12", "sectionLabel": "Key findings", "versionLabel": "P0211 · Q2 2025", "referencePeriod": "Q2 2025 (April–June 2025)", "sourceVersionId": "7f6529fe-625a-4ada-808e-78d62ccf97a1"}}]', 'The official unemployment rate in South Africa was 33.2% for the labour force aged 15–64 in the second quarter of 2025. The expanded unemployment rate was 42.9% for the labour force aged 15–64 including discouraged work-seekers in the second quarter of 2025. The number of unemployed persons aged 15–64 was 8.4 million in the second quarter of 2025.', '{}', '{"How many unemployed persons were there in South Africa in Q2 2025?","What was the headline CPI inflation rate in September 2025?","What was the real GDP growth rate in the second quarter of 2025?"}', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL, 'f949a04b-4301-40bf-b601-1d8c4865d253', '{"evidence_count": 6, "proposal_decision": "answer"}', 'Google Gemini (direct API key)', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 'ask-2026-09-1', 15966, 'none', NULL, false, '2026-09-18 07:31:28.496098+00');
